Fonts bundled with ave
======================

Every file in this directory is compiled into the binary by
src/gui/font.rs (include_bytes!). None is a crate, so cargo-deny does not
see them; this file is the record of where each came from and under which
licence, and each licence's full text ships beside the font it covers.

Mona Sans (MonaSans-Regular.ttf, MonaSans-Medium.ttf, MonaSans-SemiBold.ttf)
  Source:   https://github.com/github/mona-sans, release v2.0.27,
            mona-sans-static-v2.0.27.zip, fonts/static/ttf/
  Licence:  SIL Open Font License 1.1, MonaSans-OFL.txt
  Use:      the UI face; Medium for headers, SemiBold for buttons.

Roboto Mono (RobotoMono-Regular.ttf)
  Source:   https://github.com/googlefonts/RobotoMono, commit
            7bf0b33178844cc7d0c9915b746ece1be7f46bea, fonts/ttf/
  Licence:  SIL Open Font License 1.1, RobotoMono-OFL.txt
  Use:      monospace: timecode, tokens, code.

Lucide (Lucide.ttf)
  Source:   npm package lucide-static 1.60.0, font/lucide.ttf
            (https://unpkg.com/lucide-static@1.60.0/font/lucide.ttf);
            codepoints from font/codepoints.json of the same version.
  Licence:  ISC, with the icons derived from Feather under MIT;
            both texts in Lucide-LICENSE.txt.
  Use:      every icon in the app (src/gui/ui/icons.rs).

Inter (Inter-Regular.ttf)
  Source:   https://github.com/rsms/inter, release v4.1
  Licence:  SIL Open Font License 1.1, OFL.txt
  Use:      fallback text face behind Mona Sans.

The OFL allows bundling a font inside software provided the licence
travels with it and the font is not sold on its own. ISC and MIT require
only that the copyright and permission notices travel with it.
